      <div class="article-title">Regulation Set M-C (Updated on September 9)</div>
      <hr>
      <div class="article-body">
        Announcing Regulation Set M-C for Ranked Battles!<br /> <br /> <h1>Regulation Set M-C Duration</h1> Wednesday, September 9, 2026, at 02:00 UTC to Wednesday, December 2, 2026, at 01:59 UTC<br /> <br /> <h1>Regulation Set M-C Details</h1> <h2>Eligible Pokémon</h2> Of the Pokémon available in Pokémon Champions, only the Pokémon displayed in <b>Eligible Pokémon</b> below are eligible to participate.<br /> <br /> <a class="btn-link" href="https://web-view.app.pokemonchampions.jp/battle/pages/events/rs178713870219xeaaio/en/pokemon.html">Eligible Pokémon</a><br /> <h2>Mechanics</h2> Certain Pokémon can Mega Evolve if they’re holding a Mega Stone.<br /> <br /> You can use Mega Evolution only one time per battle.<br /> <br /> The following Mega Evolutions are newly allowed under this regulation.<br /> <h4>• Mega Absol Z<br /> • Mega Salamence<br /> • Mega Garchomp Z<br /> • Mega Lucario Z<br /> • Mega Golisopod<br /> • Mega Baxcalibur</h4> <h2>Held Items</h2> Duplicate held items are not allowed.<br /> <br /> <h2>Timers</h2> Total Time: 20 minutes<br /> Player Time: 7 minutes<br /> Turn Time: 45 seconds<br /> Preview Time: 90 seconds<br /> <br /> <h1>What Are Regulations?</h1> Regulations are the rules that govern things like which Pokémon species and held items are allowed in battle.
        <a href="../list" class="btn-link button-primary back-button">More News</a>
